  "enhanced_information": "Adding insulin glargine in a diabetic patient increases insulin levels, enhancing glucose uptake and storage while reducing blood glucose. This leads to decreased glycolysis, increased glycogenesis, decreased lipolysis, and decreased gluconeogenesis, aligning with the metabolic effects described in option opd (↓ ↑ ↓ ↑).",
